; E1, the pipe. A static archive with a C-callable interface and nothing else.
;
; `foreign_stubs` compiles retrainer_stubs.c INTO the archive, so the C++ side links
; one library rather than a library plus a loose object. The stubs are hand-written
; CAMLprim, not ctypes: every crossing is a reviewable piece of source rather than a
; generated one, which is the argument `flight/` already makes for being a hand-written
; transcription held to a reference (`docs/MODELS.md` 47.6).
;
; (!) `(modules retrainer)` IS LOAD-BEARING, AND ITS ABSENCE BROKE THIS BUILD.
; Without it dune takes EVERY `.ml` beside this file into the archive -- the
; whole Stage 48-72 ladder, which is driver and evidence code, not the pipe.
; It stayed invisible while every ladder module happened to compile with no
; library beyond the stdlib, and stopped being invisible at Stage 63:
; `zalloc_u.ml` reaches `Stdlib_upstream_compatible.Float_u`, which the ladder
; builds with `-I +stdlib_upstream_compatible` (`scripts/oxcaml_s63.sh:30`) and
; this stanza never declared, so `scripts/oxcaml_e1.sh` failed with
; "Unbound module Stdlib_upstream_compatible" in a file E1 does not use.
; Naming the one module the archive is for restores the first line's claim.
(library
 (name retrainer)
 (modes native)
 (modules acc acc_int retrainer)
 (foreign_stubs
  (language c)
  (names retrainer_stubs)))
